elopers.htm#tab-7) * [Similar Occupations](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-8) * [More Info](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-9) ## Summary Please enable javascript to play this video. ![Image 8: YouTube Video](https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_WQ_VV4pXPc/hqdefault.jpg) [Video transcript available at https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_WQ_VV4pXPc.](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_WQ_VV4pXPc) | Quick Facts: Software Developers,"}
{"source_id": "CP-S003", "chunk_id": "CP-S003-0003", "chunk_index": 2, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Software Developers", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["software", "skills", "wages", "outlook"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.718805+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "6: Occupational Outlook Handbook](https://www.bls.gov/images/ooh/ooh_title_image.png)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/) [Occupational Outlook Handbook](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/home.htm)>[Computer and Information Technology](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/home.htm)> # Software Developers, Quality Assurance Analysts, and Testers [PRINTER-FRIENDLY ![Image 7: Print](https://www.bls.gov/images/icons/icon_small_printer.gif)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#) * [Summary](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-1) * [What They Do](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-2) * [Work Environment](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-3) * [How to Become One](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-4) * [Pay](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-5) * [Job Outlook](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-6) * [State & Area Data](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-7) * [Similar Occupations](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-8) * [More Info](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-9) ## Summary Please enable javascript to play this video. ![Image 8: YouTube Video](https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_WQ_VV4pXPc/hqdefault.jpg) [Video transcript available at https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_WQ_VV4pXPc.](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_WQ_VV4pXPc) | Quick Facts: Software Developers, Quality Assurance Analysts, and Testers | | --- | | [2025 Median Pay](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=qf-wage) | $134,040 per year $64.44 per hour | | [Typical Entry-Level Education](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=qf-education) | Bachelor's degree | | [Work Experience in a Related Occupation](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=qf-experience) | None | | [On-the-job Training](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=qf-training) | None | | [Number of Jobs, 2025](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=qf-number-jobs) | 1,905,400 | | [Job Outlook, 2025–35](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=qf-outlook) | 10% (Much faster than average) | | [Employment Change, 2025–35](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=qf-emp-change) | 185,400 | ### [What Software Developers, Quality Assurance Analysts, and Testers Do](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-2) Software developers design computer applications or programs. Software quality assurance analysts and testers identify problems with applications or programs and report defects. ### [Work Environment](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-3) Many software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers work in computer systems design and related services, in manufacturing, or for software publishers. They often work in offices and on teams with other software developers or quality assurance analysts and testers. ### [How to Become a Software Developer, Quality Assurance Analyst, or Tester](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-4) Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers typically need a bachelor’s degree in computer and information technology or a related field. Some employers prefer to hire developers who have a master’s degree. ### [Pay](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-5) The median annual wage for software developers was $135,980 in May 2025. The median annual wage for software quality assurance analysts and testers was $104,300 in May 2025. ### [Job Outlook](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-6) Overall employment of software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers is projected to grow 10 percent from 2025 to 2035, much faster than the average for all occupations. About 106,100 openings for software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers are projected each year, on average, over the decade. Many of those openings are expected to result from the need to replace workers who transfer to different occupations or exit the labor force, such as to retire. ### [State & Area Data](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-7) Explore resources for employment and wages by state and area for software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers. ### [Similar Occupations](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-8) Compare the job duties, education, job growth, and pay of software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers with similar occupations. ### [More Information, Including Links to O*NET](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-9) Learn more about software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers by visiting additional resources, including O*NET, a source on key characteristics of workers"}
{"source_id": "CP-S003", "chunk_id": "CP-S003-0004", "chunk_index": 3, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Software Developers", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["software", "skills", "wages", "outlook"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.718805+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "[State & Area Data](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-7) Explore resources for employment and wages by state and area for software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers. ### [Similar Occupations](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-8) Compare the job duties, education, job growth, and pay of software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers with similar occupations. ### [More Information, Including Links to O*NET](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-9) Learn more about software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers by visiting additional resources, including O*NET, a source on key characteristics of workers and occupations. [What They Do ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-2) ## What Software Developers, Quality Assurance Analysts, and Testers Do[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-what-they-do) ![Image 9: Software developers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/1794.jpg) Developers create diagrams that help programmers write computer code. Software developers create the computer applications that allow users to do specific tasks and the underlying systems that run the devices or control networks. Software quality assurance analysts and testers design and execute software tests to identify problems and learn how the software works. ### Duties Software developers typically do the following: * Analyze users’ needs and then design and develop software to meet those needs * Recommend software upgrades for customers’ existing programs and systems * Design each piece of an application or system and plan how the pieces will work together * Create a variety of models and diagrams showing programmers the software code needed for an application * Ensure that a program continues to function normally through software maintenance and testing * Document every aspect of an application or system as a reference for future maintenance and upgrades Software quality assurance analysts and testers typically do the following: * Create test plans, scenarios, and procedures for new software * Identify project risks and recommend steps to minimize those risks * Implement software testing, using either manual or automated programs and exploratory testing, and evaluate results * Document and report defects or problems with software * Provide feedback to software developers and stakeholders regarding usability and functionality Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers are involved in the entire process of creating a software program. Developers may begin by asking how the customer plans to use the software so that they can identify the core functionality the user needs. Software developers also determine other requirements, such as security. They design the program and then work closely with [programmers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-programmers.htm), who write computer code. However, some developers write code themselves instead of giving instructions to programmers. Software quality assurance analysts and testers design and execute systems to check the software for problems. As part of their testing, these workers document and track the software’s potential defects or risks. They also assess its usability and functionality to identify difficulties a user might have. After completing testing, they report the results to software or [web developers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/web-developers.htm)"}
{"source_id": "CP-S003", "chunk_id": "CP-S003-0005", "chunk_index": 4, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Software Developers", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["software", "skills", "wages", "outlook"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.718805+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "[programmers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-programmers.htm), who write computer code. However, some developers write code themselves instead of giving instructions to programmers. Software quality assurance analysts and testers design and execute systems to check the software for problems. As part of their testing, these workers document and track the software’s potential defects or risks. They also assess its usability and functionality to identify difficulties a user might have. After completing testing, they report the results to software or [web developers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/web-developers.htm) and review ways to solve any problems they found. After the program is released to the customer, a developer may perform upgrades and maintenance. Quality assurance analysts and testers run manual and automated checks to look for errors and usability problems once the software is released and after any upgrades or maintenance. The following are examples of types of software developers: **_Applications software developers_** design computer applications, such as games, for consumers. They may create custom software for a specific customer or commercial software to be sold to the general public. Some applications software developers create databases or programs for use internally or online. **_Software engineers_** take a broad view of a project’s system and software requirements, planning its scope and order of work. These workers may direct software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers. **_Systems software developers_** create the operating systems for the public or specifically for an organization. These operating systems keep computers functioning and control most of the consumer electronics in use today, including those in cell phones and cars. Often, systems software developers also build the interface that allows users to interact with the computer. Developers who supervise a software project from the planning stages through implementation sometimes are called information technology (IT) project managers. These workers monitor the project’s progress to ensure that it meets deadlines, standards, and cost targets. For information on IT project managers who plan and direct an organization’s IT department or IT policies, see the profile on [computer and information systems (CIS) managers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/computer-and-information-systems-managers.htm). [<- Summary](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-1)[Work Environment ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-3) ## Work Environment[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-working-environment) ![Image 10: Software developers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/1795.jpg) Developers may oversee a team of people during the software development process. Software developers held about 1.7 million jobs in 2025. Some of the largest employers of software developers were as follows: Computer systems design and related services 29% Finance and insurance 11 Software publishers 10 Manufacturing 8 Management of companies and enterprises 6 Software quality assurance analysts and testers held about 187,600 jobs in 2025. Some of the largest employers of software quality assurance analysts and testers were as follows: Computer systems design and related services 30% Finance and insurance 13 Software publishers 9 Manufacturing 9 Administrative and support services 6 Developing software is usually a collaborative process. As"}
{"source_id": "CP-S003", "chunk_id": "CP-S003-0006", "chunk_index": 5, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Software Developers", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["software", "skills", "wages", "outlook"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.718805+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "and related services 29% Finance and insurance 11 Software publishers 10 Manufacturing 8 Management of companies and enterprises 6 Software quality assurance analysts and testers held about 187,600 jobs in 2025. Some of the largest employers of software quality assurance analysts and testers were as follows: Computer systems design and related services 30% Finance and insurance 13 Software publishers 9 Manufacturing 9 Administrative and support services 6 Developing software is usually a collaborative process. As a result, developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers work on teams with others who also contribute to designing, developing, and programming successful software. ### Work Schedules Most software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers work full time. [<- What They Do](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-2)[How to Become One ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-4) ## How to Become a Software Developer, Quality Assurance Analyst, or Tester[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-become-one) ![Image 11: Software developers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/3638.jpg) Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers typically need a bachelor’s degree. Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers typically need a bachelor’s degree in computer and information technology or a related field. Some employers prefer to hire developers who have a master’s degree. ### Education Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers typically need a bachelor's[degree](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/field-of-degree/home.htm)in[computer and information technology](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/field-of-degree/computer-and-information/computer-and-information-technology-field-of-degree.htm)or a related field, such as[engineering](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/field-of-degree/engineering/engineering-field-of-degree.htm)or[mathematics](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/field-of-degree/mathematics/mathematics-field-of-degree.htm). Computer and information technology degree programs cover a broad range of topics. Students may gain experience in software development by completing an internship, such as at a software company, while in college. For some software developer positions, employers may prefer that applicants have a master’s degree. Although writing code is not their primary responsibility, developers must have a strong background in computer programming. They usually gain this experience in school. Throughout their career, developers must keep up to date on new tools and computer languages. ### Advancement Software developers can advance to become project management specialists or [computer and information systems managers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/computer-and-information-systems-managers.htm \"Computer and Information Systems Managers\"), positions in which they oversee the software development process. ### Important Qualities The following are examples of qualities that are important for these workers to perform their duties. For more information, visit the Employment Projections (EP) [skills data page](https://www.bls.gov/emp/data/skills-data.htm). **_Analytical skills._** Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers must evaluate users’ needs and then design software to function properly and meet those needs. **_Communication skills_**. These workers must be able to give clear instructions and explain problems that arise to other team members involved in development. They must also be able to explain to nontechnical users, such as customers, how the software works and answer any questions that arise. **_Creativity._** Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers must be innovative in their approaches to designing, identifying problems with, and improving computer software. **_Detail oriented._** These workers often need to concentrate"}
{"source_id": "CP-S003", "chunk_id": "CP-S003-0007", "chunk_index": 6, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Software Developers", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["software", "skills", "wages", "outlook"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.718805+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "These workers must be able to give clear instructions and explain problems that arise to other team members involved in development. They must also be able to explain to nontechnical users, such as customers, how the software works and answer any questions that arise. **_Creativity._** Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers must be innovative in their approaches to designing, identifying problems with, and improving computer software. **_Detail oriented._** These workers often need to concentrate on many parts of an application or system at the same time, and they must pay attention to detail when looking for potential areas of user error. **_Interpersonal skills._** Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers must be able to work well with others who contribute to designing, programming, and testing successful software. **_Problem-solving skills._** Because these workers produce software from beginning to end, they must be able to solve problems that arise throughout the design process. [<- Work Environment](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-3)[Pay ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-5) ## Pay[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-pay) ### Software Developers, Quality Assurance Analysts, and Testers Median annual wages, May 2025 Software developers $135,980 Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers $134,040 Computer occupations $109,470 Software quality assurance analysts and testers $104,300 Total, all occupations $50,980 Note: Data are from the Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics program. All Occupations includes all occupations in the U.S. Economy. Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. The median annual wage for software developers was $135,980 in May 2025. The median wage is the wage at which half the workers in an occupation earned more than that amount and half earned less. The lowest 10 percent earned less than $82,460, and the highest 10 percent earned more than $214,670. The median annual wage for software quality assurance analysts and testers was $104,300 in May 2025. The lowest 10 percent earned less than $61,440, and the highest 10 percent earned more than $167,010. In May 2025, the median annual wages for software developers in some of the top industries in which they worked were as follows: Software publishers$164,550 Manufacturing 136,330 Management of companies and enterprises 135,680 Finance and insurance 135,460 Computer systems design and related services 132,050 In May 2025, the median annual wages for software quality assurance analysts and testers in some of the top industries in which they worked were as follows: Manufacturing$129,930 Finance and insurance 104,260 Administrative and support services 102,660 Software publishers 101,070 Computer systems design and related services 99,960 Most software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers work full time. [<- How to Become One](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-4)[Job Outlook ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-6) ## Job Outlook[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-job-outlook) ### Software Developers, Quality Assurance Analysts, and Testers Percent change in employment, projected 2025–35 Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers 10% Software developers 10% Computer occupations"}
{"source_id": "CP-S003", "chunk_id": "CP-S003-0008", "chunk_index": 7, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Software Developers", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["software", "skills", "wages", "outlook"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.718805+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "they worked were as follows: Manufacturing$129,930 Finance and insurance 104,260 Administrative and support services 102,660 Software publishers 101,070 Computer systems design and related services 99,960 Most software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers work full time. [<- How to Become One](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-4)[Job Outlook ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-6) ## Job Outlook[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-job-outlook) ### Software Developers, Quality Assurance Analysts, and Testers Percent change in employment, projected 2025–35 Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers 10% Software developers 10% Computer occupations 6% Software quality assurance analysts and testers 6% Total, all occupations 3% Note: Percent change in employment is rounded to the nearest whole number. All Occupations includes all occupations in the U.S. Economy. Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. Overall employment of software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers is projected to grow 10 percent from 2025 to 2035, much faster than the average for all occupations. About 106,100 openings for software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers are projected each year, on average, over the decade. Many of those openings are expected to result from the need to replace workers who transfer to different occupations or exit the labor force, such as to retire. ### Employment Demand for software developers, software quality assurance analysts, and testers is projected to be strong due to the continued expansion of software development for artificial intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), robotics, and other automation applications. In response to concerns over threats to computer security, organizations are expected to increase investment in software that protects their electronic networks and infrastructure. This investment could result in an increased demand for developers to create security software and for quality assurance analysts and testers to create and execute software tests. Software developers, software quality assurance analysts, and testers are likely to see new opportunities because of the increasing number of products that use software. For example, software systems continue to be built for consumer electronics and other products, including IoT-connected devices and electric vehicles (EVs). Employment projections data for software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers, 2025–35 | Occupational Title | SOC Code | Employment, 2025 | Projected Employment, 2035 | Change, 2025–35 | Employment by Industry | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | Percent | Numeric | | Note: Employment subcategories do not necessarily add to higher categories due to rounding. Employment and projected employment change values are rounded to the nearest 100 or percent. Data is unavailable for values denoted with a \"—\". Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. | | **Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers** | — | 1,905,400 | 2,090,800 | 10 | 185,400 | — | | **Software developers** | 15-1252 | 1,717,800 | 1,892,600 |"}
{"source_id": "CP-S003", "chunk_id": "CP-S003-0009", "chunk_index": 8, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Software Developers", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["software", "skills", "wages", "outlook"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.718805+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "| Note: Employment subcategories do not necessarily add to higher categories due to rounding. Employment and projected employment change values are rounded to the nearest 100 or percent. Data is unavailable for values denoted with a \"—\". Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. | | **Software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers** | — | 1,905,400 | 2,090,800 | 10 | 185,400 | — | | **Software developers** | 15-1252 | 1,717,800 | 1,892,600 | 10 | 174,700 | [Get data](https://data.bls.gov/projections/nationalMatrix?queryParams=15-1252&ioType=o) | | **Software quality assurance analysts and testers** | 15-1253 | 187,600 | 198,200 | 6 | 10,600 | [Get data](https://data.bls.gov/projections/nationalMatrix?queryParams=15-1253&ioType=o) | [<- Pay](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-5)[State & Area Data ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-7) ## State & Area Data[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-state-area) ### **Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (OEWS)** The [Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics](https://www.bls.gov/oes/) (OEWS) program produces employment and wage estimates annually for over 800 occupations. These estimates are available for the nation as a whole, for individual states, and for metropolitan and nonmetropolitan areas. The link below goes to OEWS data maps for employment and wages by state and area. Use the dropdown boxes to select an occupation. * [Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (OEWS) Profiles](https://data.bls.gov/oesprofile/) ### **Projections Central** Occupational employment projections are developed for all states by Labor Market Information (LMI) or individual state Employment Projections offices. All state projections data are available at [https://projectionscentral.org](https://projectionscentral.org/). Information on this site allows projected employment growth for an occupation to be compared among states or to be compared within one state. In addition, states may produce projections for areas; there are links to each state’s websites where these data may be retrieved. ### **CareerOneStop** CareerOneStop includes hundreds of [occupational profiles](http://www.careerinfonet.org/Occupations/select_occupation.aspx?next=occ_rep&level=&optstatus=111111111&id=1&nodeid=2&soccode=&stfips=&jobfam=&menuMode) with data available by state and metro area. There are links in the left-hand side menu to compare occupational employment by state and occupational wages by local area or metro area. There is also a [salary info tool](https://www.careeronestop.org/Toolkit/Wages/find-salary.aspx?frd=true) to search for wages by zip code. [<- Job Outlook](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-6)[Similar Occupations ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#tab-8) ## Similar Occupations[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-similar-jobs) This table shows a list of occupations with job duties that are similar to those of software developers, quality assurance analysts, and testers. | | Occupation | Job Duties | ENTRY-LEVEL EDUCATION [![Image 12: Help on Median Pay](https://www.bls.gov/images/icons/icon_small_help.gif)](https://www.bls.gov/#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=inlinehelp-education) | 2025 MEDIAN PAY [![Image 13: Help on Median Pay](https://www.bls.gov/images/icons/icon_small_help.gif)](https://www.bls.gov/#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=inlinehelp-pay) | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | [![Image 14: Computer and information research scientists](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/1504.jpg)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-and-information-research-scientists.htm) | **[Computer and Information Research Scientists](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-and-information-research-scientists.htm)** | Computer and information research scientists design innovative uses for new and existing computing technology. | Master's degree | $140,300 | | [![Image 15: Computer and information systems managers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/1597.jpg)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/computer-and-information-systems-managers.htm) | **[Computer and Information Systems Managers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/computer-and-information-systems-managers.htm)** | Computer and information systems managers plan, coordinate, and direct computer-related activities"}
