cal level of education that most workers need to enter this occupation. ## Work experience in a related occupation Work experience that is commonly considered necessary by employers, or is a commonly accepted substitute for more formal types of training or education. ## Number of Jobs, 2025 The employment, or size, of this occupation in 2025, which is the base year of the 2025–35 employment projections. ## Job Outlook, 2025-35 The projected percent change in employment from 2025 to 2035. The average growth rate for all occupations is 3 percent. ## Employment Change, 2025-35 The projected numeric change in employment from 2025 to 2035. ## Entry-level Education Typical level of education that most workers need to enter this occupation. ## On-the-job Training Additional training needed (postemployment) to attain competency in the skills needed in this occupation. ## Employment Change, projected 2025-35 The projected numeric change in employment from 2025 to 2035. ## Growth Rate (Projected) The percent change of employment for each occupation from 2025 to 2035. ## Projected Number of New Jobs The projected numeric change in employment from 2025 to 2035. ## Projected Growth Rate The projected percent change in employment from 2025 to 2035. ## 2025 Median Pay The wage at which half of the workers in the occupation earned more than that amount and half earned less. Median wage data are from the BLS Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics survey. In May 2025, the median annual wage for all"}
