{"source_id": "CP-S007", "chunk_id": "CP-S007-0008", "chunk_index": 7, "publisher": "BLS", "title": "Computer Systems Analysts", "category": "occupations", "topics": ["systems", "analysis", "skills"], "url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm", "resolved_url": "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm", "retrieval_method": "reader_fallback", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:41.719572+00:00", "http_status": 403, "content_type": "text/plain", "word_count": 450, "text": "denoted with a \"—\". Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. | | **Computer systems analysts** | 15-1211 | 544,400 | 587,200 | 8 | 42,900 | [Get data](https://data.bls.gov/projections/nationalMatrix?queryParams=15-1211&ioType=o) | [<- Pay](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm#tab-5)[State & Area Data ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm#tab-7) ## State & Area Data[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-state-area) ### **Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (OEWS)** The [Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics](https://www.bls.gov/oes/) (OEWS) program produces employment and wage estimates annually for over 800 occupations. These estimates are available for the nation as a whole, for individual states, and for metropolitan and nonmetropolitan areas. The link below goes to OEWS data maps for employment and wages by state and area. Use the dropdown boxes to select an occupation. * [Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (OEWS) Profiles](https://data.bls.gov/oesprofile/) ### **Projections Central** Occupational employment projections are developed for all states by Labor Market Information (LMI) or individual state Employment Projections offices. All state projections data are available at [https://projectionscentral.org](https://projectionscentral.org/). Information on this site allows projected employment growth for an occupation to be compared among states or to be compared within one state. In addition, states may produce projections for areas; there are links to each state’s websites where these data may be retrieved. ### **CareerOneStop** CareerOneStop includes hundreds of [occupational profiles](http://www.careerinfonet.org/Occupations/select_occupation.aspx?next=occ_rep&level=&optstatus=111111111&id=1&nodeid=2&soccode=&stfips=&jobfam=&menuMode) with data available by state and metro area. There are links in the left-hand side menu to compare occupational employment by state and occupational wages by local area or metro area. There is also a [salary info tool](https://www.careeronestop.org/Toolkit/Wages/find-salary.aspx?frd=true) to search for wages by zip code. [<- Job Outlook](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm#tab-6)[Similar Occupations ->](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm#tab-8) ## Similar Occupations[About this section](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-systems-analysts.htm#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=about-similar-jobs) This table shows a list of occupations with job duties that are similar to those of computer systems analysts. | | Occupation | Job Duties | ENTRY-LEVEL EDUCATION [![Image 12: Help on Median Pay](https://www.bls.gov/images/icons/icon_small_help.gif)](https://www.bls.gov/#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=inlinehelp-education) | 2025 MEDIAN PAY [![Image 13: Help on Median Pay](https://www.bls.gov/images/icons/icon_small_help.gif)](https://www.bls.gov/#TB_inline?height=325&width=325&inlineId=inlinehelp-pay) | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | [![Image 14: Actuaries](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/1828.jpg)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/math/actuaries.htm) | **[Actuaries](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/math/actuaries.htm)** | Actuaries use mathematics, statistics, and financial theory to analyze the economic costs of risk and uncertainty. | Bachelor's degree | $130,000 | | [![Image 15: Computer and information research scientists](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/1504.jpg)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-and-information-research-scientists.htm) | **[Computer and Information Research Scientists](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-and-information-research-scientists.htm)** | Computer and information research scientists design innovative uses for new and existing computing technology. | Master's degree | $140,300 | | [![Image 16: Computer and information systems managers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/1597.jpg)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/computer-and-information-systems-managers.htm) | **[Computer and Information Systems Managers](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/computer-and-information-systems-managers.htm)** | Computer and information systems managers plan, coordinate, and direct computer-related activities in an organization. | Bachelor's degree | $175,140 | | [![Image 17: computer network architects image](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/images/15198.jpg)](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-network-architects.htm) | **[Computer Network Architects](https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/computer-network-architects.htm)** | Computer network architects design and implement data communication networks, including local area networks (LANs), wide area networks (WANs), and intranets. | Bachelor's degree | $134,050 | | [![Image"}
