nd ideas presented through spoken words and sentences. Related occupations Number Facility — The ability to add, subtract, multiply, or divide quickly and correctly. Related occupations Oral Expression — The ability to communicate information and ideas in speaking so others will understand. Related occupations Speech Clarity — The ability to speak clearly so others can understand you. Related occupations Flexibility of Closure — The ability to identify or detect a known pattern (a figure, object, word, or sound) that is hidden in other distracting material. Related occupations Originality — The ability to come up with unusual or clever ideas about a given topic or situation, or to develop creative ways to solve a problem. Related occupations Selective Attention — The ability to concentrate on a task over a period of time without being distracted. Related occupations Speech Recognition — The ability to identify and understand the speech of another person. Related occupations Fluency of Ideas — The ability to come up with a number of ideas about a topic (the number of ideas is important, not their quality, correctness, or creativity). Related occupations Speed of Closure — The ability to quickly make sense of, combine, and organize information into meaningful patterns. Related occupations back to top Interests All 2 displayed Interest code: IC Want to discover your interests? Take the"}
