{"source_id": "CP-S062", "chunk_id": "CP-S062-0001", "chunk_index": 0, "publisher": "Microsoft Careers", "title": "Microsoft Careers", "category": "employer", "topics": ["careers", "technology"], "url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/", "resolved_url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/home.html", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:54.938248+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 153, "text": "Home | Microsoft Careers https://uhf.microsoft.com/en-US/shell/xml/MSActionCenter?headerId=GlobalCareersPCSHeaderprod&footerid=CareersPCSFooterprod https://careers.microsoft.com/bin/msft/searchheader https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/sign-in.html https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/ca/fr/connexion.html https://cdn.careers.microsoft.com/aem/asset-manifest.json 654c6aaa25ad4751986d2b4fdcf3da6f-b7d405fc-078f-42fd-99cf-e21de3479349-7421 https://gcssupportuippe.azureedge.net/asset-manifest.json PROD https://uhf.microsoft.com/fr-CA/shell/xml/MSActionCenter?headerId=GlobalCareersPCSHeaderprod&footerid=CareersPCSFooterprod PROD https://apply.careers.microsoft.com/careers Win and thrive together  ✖  ✖ Find jobs Empowered by Purpose. United by Mission When you join Microsoft, you’re not just stepping into a job— you’re stepping into a mission-driven company where purpose is at the heart of everything we do. Our mission—to empower every person and every organization on the planet to achieve more—isn’t just words. It’s our foundation. It’s what sets us apart. Life at Microsoft Benefits Explore Microsoft’s world-class benefits designed to help you and your family live well. Culture We will only achieve our mission if we live our culture, which starts with applying a growth mindset. Diversity and inclusion We are committed to celebrating the diversity around us and its power to drive us forward together. Hiring Tips Explore resources to help you prepare—Microsoft is here to support your interview journey."}
{"source_id": "CP-S063", "chunk_id": "CP-S063-0001", "chunk_index": 0, "publisher": "Microsoft Careers", "title": "Students and Graduates", "category": "internships", "topics": ["internships", "students"], "url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "resolved_url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:54.947240+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "Early in profession | Microsoft Careers https://uhf.microsoft.com/en-US/shell/xml/MSActionCenter?headerId=GlobalCareersPCSHeaderprod&footerid=CareersPCSFooterprod https://careers.microsoft.com/bin/msft/searchheader https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/sign-in.html https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/ca/fr/connexion.html https://cdn.careers.microsoft.com/aem/asset-manifest.json 654c6aaa25ad4751986d2b4fdcf3da6f-b7d405fc-078f-42fd-99cf-e21de3479349-7421 https://gcssupportuippe.azureedge.net/asset-manifest.json PROD https://uhf.microsoft.com/fr-CA/shell/xml/MSActionCenter?headerId=GlobalCareersPCSHeaderprod&footerid=CareersPCSFooterprod PROD https://apply.careers.microsoft.com/careers Early in profession  ✖  ✖ Find jobs Empowered to learn. Inspired to contribute At Microsoft, your career begins with possibility. Our Early in Profession opportunities are designed to help you grow with purpose—supported by teams working together to empower people and communities around the world. Whether you're joining from school, a bootcamp, or a career pivot, you’ll be part of a collective effort where every role contributes to meaningful outcomes—and you’ll be invited to learn, collaborate, and build alongside others. We know that growth isn’t linear. It comes from putting in the effort to do your best work, taking ownership of your path, and staying open to learning and evolving. That’s why we encourage thoughtful risks and learning through action. When missteps happen, we treat them as opportunities to reflect, adapt, and move forward—because progress is built on accountability and resilience. You’ll be guided by mentors and managers who help you shape your goals and stretch your potential. And as you grow, you’ll discover that your impact can ripple across teams, communities, and industries. Starting your career at Microsoft means joining a culture of shared success—where collaboration fuels innovation, and your journey can lead to endless possibilities. Internship programs Global university internships At Microsoft, our interns work on projects that matter – and your team will rely on your skills and insights to help deliver those projects to market. This is your chance to bring your solutions and ideas to life while working on cutting-edge technology. We offer internships in all job families and solution areas, and it’s open to current students in Bachelor’s, Master’s, MBA, PhD programs. Discovery program The Discovery Program is a unique opportunity for students who are passionate about technology and want to make a positive impact on the world and society. This four-week internship is open to rising first-year students college students, based in Redmond, Washington or Atlanta, Georgia. Participants will work on a real project, learn from Microsoft employees and mentors, and explore different career paths in tech. Explore program Explore Microsoft is a summer internship program specifically designed for first- and/or second-year college students. Gain experience in software development through a learning program where you get the opportunity to work in a pod alongside other Explore Interns. PhD, MBA, JD internships If you're pursuing a PhD, MBA, or JD and want to explore what it's like to work at Microsoft, look no further. We host PhD, MBA, and JD interns throughout our teams. Our PhD, MBA, and JD interns are active, contributing members to our community. No matter what route you take, come work"}
{"source_id": "CP-S063", "chunk_id": "CP-S063-0002", "chunk_index": 1, "publisher": "Microsoft Careers", "title": "Students and Graduates", "category": "internships", "topics": ["internships", "students"], "url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "resolved_url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:54.947240+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "through a learning program where you get the opportunity to work in a pod alongside other Explore Interns. PhD, MBA, JD internships If you're pursuing a PhD, MBA, or JD and want to explore what it's like to work at Microsoft, look no further. We host PhD, MBA, and JD interns throughout our teams. Our PhD, MBA, and JD interns are active, contributing members to our community. No matter what route you take, come work on meaningful, innovative projects that add to our company's success. Corporate, External, and Legal Affairs (CELA) internships The Microsoft Legal Intern Program is an extraordinary opportunity for aspiring legal professionals to cultivate their careers within one of the world's leading technology companies. Rotation programs HR Rotation Finance Rotation Cloud Supply Chain Rotation Our HR rotation program is a 3-year program that fosters learning and growth in the HR profession and helps you jumpstart your career. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/hrrotation Learn more about the HR2P program Our Microsoft Finance Rotation Program (FRP) is a two-year program comprised of four, 6-month rotations, split across core finance functions. Kick-start your career in finance with a rotation in corporate functions, production/engineering finance, sales finance and more. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/financerotation Learn more about the finance rotation program SCORE is a three-year career experience designed to provide emerging talent with an unparalleled journey through end-to-end cloud supply chain operations. Over three one-year rotations, participants will partner with and learn from our teams while building skills and supply chain acumen to accelerate their career growth. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/score.html Learn more about the supply chain rotation program HR Rotation Finance Rotation Cloud Supply Chain Rotation Our HR rotation program is a 3-year program that fosters learning and growth in the HR profession and helps you jumpstart your career. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/hrrotation Learn more about the HR2P program Our Microsoft Finance Rotation Program (FRP) is a two-year program comprised of four, 6-month rotations, split across core finance functions. Kick-start your career in finance with a rotation in corporate functions, production/engineering finance, sales finance and more. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/financerotation Learn more about the finance rotation program SCORE is a three-year career experience designed to provide emerging talent with an unparalleled journey through end-to-end cloud supply chain operations. Over three one-year rotations, participants will partner with and learn from our teams while building skills and supply chain acumen to accelerate their career growth. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/score.html Learn more about the supply chain rotation program ❮ Microsoft Customer and Partner Solutions Early in Profession Program (MCAPS EiP) The world is interested in AI and the world trusts Microsoft as their partner for AI transformation. Microsoft Customer and Partner Solutions (MCAPS) is the company's global unified commercial organization with responsibility for global strategy and sales execution. That’s our fancy way of"}
{"source_id": "CP-S063", "chunk_id": "CP-S063-0003", "chunk_index": 2, "publisher": "Microsoft Careers", "title": "Students and Graduates", "category": "internships", "topics": ["internships", "students"], "url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "resolved_url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:54.947240+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "building skills and supply chain acumen to accelerate their career growth. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/score.html Learn more about the supply chain rotation program ❮ Microsoft Customer and Partner Solutions Early in Profession Program (MCAPS EiP) The world is interested in AI and the world trusts Microsoft as their partner for AI transformation. Microsoft Customer and Partner Solutions (MCAPS) is the company's global unified commercial organization with responsibility for global strategy and sales execution. That’s our fancy way of saying we are making magic happen for customers and partners around the world. The MCAPS Early in Profession (EiP) program prepares the next generation of sales and technical leaders to enable AI transformation and solve mission-critical technology issues for our customers and partners. The MCAPS EiP program is a three-year program designed to accelerate your growth. From day one, you'll dive into AI-driven tools and human-powered experiences that will help you become a sales or technical leader. You'll have a curated onboarding, skilling, and career development path that prepares you to deliver meaningful results for customers and partners. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/MCAPSEIP.html Learn more about MCAPS EiP Microsoft Aspire Experience We believe that Microsoft is a place for exploration and creativity. Microsoft Aspire is a 1+ year learning and development journey designed for new full-time employees from undergraduate, masters, MBA, PhD, MSSA, or LEAP backgrounds designed to equip, develop, and empower those who are hired and start at Microsoft from a qualifying program. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/recentgraduate Learn more about Aspire ❯ Hiring programs ❮ Neurodiversity We built the Microsoft Neurodiversity Hiring Program on the belief that neurodivergent individuals strengthen a workforce with innovative thinking and creative solutions. Diverse teams positively impact our company culture, working environment and how we serve our customers. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/neurodiversity.html Learn more about the Neurodiversity Hiring Program Neurodiversity We built the Microsoft Neurodiversity Hiring Program on the belief that neurodivergent individuals strengthen a workforce with innovative thinking and creative solutions. Diverse teams positively impact our company culture, working environment and how we serve our customers. \"https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/neurodiversity.html\" \"Learn more about the Neurodiversity Hiring Program\" Leap At Microsoft, we know there are many pathways into the technology industry and into our organization. We're constantly looking for new ways to create unconventional entry points for talent and leverage the skills and experiences of talent from outside the traditional academic paths. Additional program details coming soon. Leap At Microsoft, we know there are many pathways into the technology industry and into our organization. We're constantly looking for new ways to create unconventional entry points for talent and leverage the skills and experiences of talent from outside the traditional academic paths. Additional program details coming soon. MSSA Microsoft Software and Systems Academy (MSSA) provides transitioning service members and veterans with critical technical"}
{"source_id": "CP-S063", "chunk_id": "CP-S063-0004", "chunk_index": 3, "publisher": "Microsoft Careers", "title": "Students and Graduates", "category": "internships", "topics": ["internships", "students"], "url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "resolved_url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:54.947240+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "outside the traditional academic paths. Additional program details coming soon. Leap At Microsoft, we know there are many pathways into the technology industry and into our organization. We're constantly looking for new ways to create unconventional entry points for talent and leverage the skills and experiences of talent from outside the traditional academic paths. Additional program details coming soon. MSSA Microsoft Software and Systems Academy (MSSA) provides transitioning service members and veterans with critical technical and career skills required for today’s growing technology industry. https://military.microsoft.com/mssa/ Learn more about MSSA MSSA Microsoft Software and Systems Academy (MSSA) provides transitioning service members and veterans with critical technical and career skills required for today’s growing technology industry. \"https://military.microsoft.com/mssa/\" \"Learn more about MSSA\" Student Veterans Microsoft offers internships and onboarding programs for student veterans who are working toward a degree in a STEM field. https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/military/student-veterans Learn more about our student veterans Student Veterans Microsoft offers internships and onboarding programs for student veterans who are working toward a degree in a STEM field. \"https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/military/student-veterans\" \"Learn more about our student veterans\" Datacenter pathways HaaS datacenter pathways Datacenters are the backbone of modern technology—massive warehouses filled with thousands of interconnected servers, running 24/7. Behind it all are our Datacenter Operations teams, made up of individuals from diverse backgrounds, like you, ensuring everything stays operational. It’s routine work with a remarkable impact. Learn more about our Datacenter Pathways Microsoft Datacenter Academy The Datacenter Academy empowers individuals to thrive in cloud computing, IT, and critical environments. This initiative offers a comprehensive pathway to employment in these rapidly expanding fields, providing skills for the future of technology. Learn more about the Microsoft Datacenter Academy Datacenter pathways HaaS datacenter pathways Datacenters are the backbone of modern technology—massive warehouses filled with thousands of interconnected servers, running 24/7. Behind it all are our Datacenter Operations teams, made up of individuals from diverse backgrounds, like you, ensuring everything stays operational. It’s routine work with a remarkable impact. Learn more about our Datacenter Pathways Microsoft Datacenter Academy The Datacenter Academy empowers individuals to thrive in cloud computing, IT, and critical environments. This initiative offers a comprehensive pathway to employment in these rapidly expanding fields, providing skills for the future of technology. Learn more about the Microsoft Datacenter Academy ❯ Explore EiP opportunities Digital Solution Area Specialists - PwD Opportunities 2026-08-18 Brazil, São Paulo, São Paulo 3 days / week in-office <b>Overview</b><br><p>The objective of the \"Ability Hiring Event\" is to build an inclusive hiring approach that recognizes and embraces the skills of candidates with all disabilities. The World Health Organization defines disability as arising from the interaction between a person's health condition or impairment and the many influencing factors in their environment. Health conditions associated with"}
{"source_id": "CP-S063", "chunk_id": "CP-S063-0005", "chunk_index": 4, "publisher": "Microsoft Careers", "title": "Students and Graduates", "category": "internships", "topics": ["internships", "students"], "url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "resolved_url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:54.947240+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "EiP opportunities Digital Solution Area Specialists - PwD Opportunities 2026-08-18 Brazil, São Paulo, São Paulo 3 days / week in-office <b>Overview</b><br><p>The objective of the \"Ability Hiring Event\" is to build an inclusive hiring approach that recognizes and embraces the skills of candidates with all disabilities. The World Health Organization defines disability as arising from the interaction between a person's health condition or impairment and the many influencing factors in their environment. Health conditions associated with disability may include, but are not limited to, those that are visible or invisible; temporary or long-term; static, episodic, or degenerative; painful or inconsequential.<br>If you identify as a person with a disability, you are encouraged to apply to this program. Are you eligible for this program?</p><div><p>Come build a community, explore your passions and do your best work at Microsoft. This opportunity will allow you to bring your aspirations, talent, potential, and excitement for the journey ahead. Are you inspired to empower organizations to transform the way they work by harnessing the full potential of artificial intelligence? We are seeking individuals to help guide customers through the evolving digital landscape, enabling them to unlock new opportunities, enhance productivity, and deliver exceptional employee and customer experiences. Join us integrating advanced AI capabilities across devices, cloud platforms, and everyday business applications to help organizations realize seamless, innovative, and secure solutions that drive sustained growth and success in the AI era. </p><p> </p><div><p>As a Digital Solution Area Specialist, you will lead the charge in driving AI transformation across customers by positioning Microsoft’s AI Business Solutions as strategic enablers of productivity and innovation. You will engage business decision makers through consultative selling, develop compelling business cases, and orchestrate cross-functional teams to accelerate adoption and value realization. This role empowers you to shape customer intent, build pipelines, and deliver measurable impact while deepening your expertise in AI sales motions and contributing to a high-performance, learning-driven culture. </p></div><div><p>To prepare for the role, you will be enrolled in the Early-in-Profession (EiP) Program. This program exemplifies the company’s commitment to developing early-career talent through robust onboarding and mentorship. These programs are designed to accelerate new hires’ productivity, integrate them into Microsoft’s culture, and set them on a path for long-term growth within the company. Participants in EiP benefit from a comprehensive onboarding experience that includes immersive training, structured job shadowing with colleagues, and continuous support from dedicated mentors. By investing heavily in the first six months of a new employee tenure, Microsoft ensures its early-in-career hires to build essential skills, confidence, and professional networks that will enable them to excel. </p></div><div><p>Microsoft’s mission is to empower every person and every organization on the planet to achieve more. As employees, we come together with a growth"}
{"source_id": "CP-S063", "chunk_id": "CP-S063-0006", "chunk_index": 5, "publisher": "Microsoft Careers", "title": "Students and Graduates", "category": "internships", "topics": ["internships", "students"], "url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "resolved_url": "https://careers.microsoft.com/v2/global/en/students", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:54.947240+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "a comprehensive onboarding experience that includes immersive training, structured job shadowing with colleagues, and continuous support from dedicated mentors. By investing heavily in the first six months of a new employee tenure, Microsoft ensures its early-in-career hires to build essential skills, confidence, and professional networks that will enable them to excel. </p></div><div><p>Microsoft’s mission is to empower every person and every organization on the planet to achieve more. As employees, we come together with a growth mindset, innovate to empower others, and collaborate to realize our shared goals. Each day we build on our values of respect, integrity, and accountability to create a culture of inclusion where everyone can thrive at work and beyond. </p></div></div><br><br><b>Responsibilities</b><br><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Lead consultative sales conversations with business decision makers, helping customers understand how Microsoft AI solutions can transform the way they work. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Serve as a trusted advisor by aligning AI solutions to customer business priorities, developing compelling business value and ROI cases, and guiding customers through their AI transformation journey. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Drive adoption and growth of Microsoft AI solutions by identifying opportunities to deliver measurable customer value and business outcomes. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Partner with technical specialists, engineering teams, customer success, and partner organizations to develop and execute end-to-end customer engagement and sales strategies. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Identify and develop new sales opportunities through customer engagement, marketing programs, digital insights, and partner collaboration. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Maintain accurate account plans, pipelines, and customer engagement activities to support business goals and sales execution. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Collaborate across Microsoft solution areas to deliver integrated customer solutions. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Build strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders to accelerate customer success and achieve shared business objectives. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Demonstrate Microsoft's values by operating with integrity, accountability, and a commitment to ethical business practices while proactively identifying and managing risks. </p></li></ul></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Continuously develop expertise in AI, emerging technologies, and consultative selling to deliver exceptional customer experiences. </p></li></ul></div><br><br><b>Qualifications</b><br><div><p><strong>Required / minimum qualifications </strong></p></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Bachelor's Degree in Information Technology, or related field AND 2+ years of technology-related sales or account management experience OR 3+ years of technology-related sales or account management experience. </p></li></ul></div><div><p><strong>Additional or preferred qualifications </strong></p></div><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\"><li><p>Bachelor's Degree in Information Technology, or related field AND 3+ years of technology-related sales or account management work experience OR 4+ years of technology-related sales or account management experience. </p></li><li>AI-related coursework, training, or certification from any provider or platform. </li></ul></div> <br><p>This position will be open for a minimum of 5 days, with applications accepted on an ongoing basis until the position is filled.</p><br><hr><br><p>Microsoft is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, citizenship, color, family or medical care leave, gender identity or expression, genetic information, immigration status, marital status, medical condition, national origin, physical or mental"}
