{"source_id": "CP-S067", "chunk_id": "CP-S067-0009", "chunk_index": 8, "publisher": "NVIDIA Careers", "title": "University Recruiting", "category": "internships", "topics": ["students", "internships"], "url": "https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/about-nvidia/careers/university-recruiting/", "resolved_url": "https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/about-nvidia/careers/university-recruiting/", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:56.417448+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "Video Alternatively, you can (youtubeLink)watch this video on YouTube(/youtubeLink). Consent for Optional Cookies (googleCookiePolicyLink)YouTube sets performance, advertising, and other optional cookies(/googleCookiePolicyLink) when you watch embedded videos. To watch this video, you need to turn on optional cookies for the site. By clicking “Accept and Play Video,” you will automatically turn on advertising and other optional cookies for the site and accept our (nvidiaTermsOfServiceLink)Terms of Service(/nvidiaTermsOfServiceLink) (which contains important waivers). Please see our (nvidiaPrivacyPolicyLink)Privacy Policy(/nvidiaPrivacyPolicyLink) and (nvidiaCookiePolicyLink)Cookie Policy(/nvidiaCookiePolicyLink) for more information. Cancel Accept and Play Video Alternatively, you can (youtubeLink)watch this video on YouTube(/youtubeLink). Our interns are employees. They do real work, on real projects, side by side with some of the industry's brightest minds. Interns get hands-on with never-before-seen technologies and the latest software and hardware developments. Explore Early-Talent Programs Intern Ignite MBA PhD New College Grad Being an intern is the best way to kick-start your journey at NVIDIA, as it’s our primary pipeline for new college grads and early-in-career hiring. You’ll take part in meaningful work, make a difference on real projects, connect with the greatest minds in our industry, and build lifelong connections. Whether you’re pursuing a BS, MS, PhD, or MBA, we offer year-round internships—for a minimum of 12 weeks—with great benefits. I’ve been able to talk with everyone—from executives to other interns—while exploring a variety of disciplines. Having exposure to a breadth of people and projects has been very helpful in developing skills that better my community. — David, Trustworthy AI Intern The NVIDIA Ignite program gives you everything you need to start building your career—a whole lot earlier than you might expect. This inclusive, 12-week summer pre-internship program was created to give current freshmen and sophomores from a wide range of backgrounds a chance to work hands-on with real technical experts on real projects. It’s a fully immersive experience covering the products, culture, and ecosystem that make NVIDIA a truly unique place to ignite your future. The Ignite program was a true catalyst for me. The group of people I met became a strong support system, and we’ve stayed connected ever since. That sense of community continues to motivate me. — Sergio, Ignite Intern The NVIDIA MBA program is designed to help interns and new college grads develop into the next generation of corporate leaders. Through our best-in-class programs, we also provide powerful upleveling and organic growth tools to help professionals pivot industries and pursue lifelong learning. At NVIDIA, I was given the resources, autonomy, and unwavering support to push my limits and dream bigger than ever. My team not only challenged me but also lifted me up, helping me unlock potential I never imagined I could reach in just one summer. — Paul,"}
{"source_id": "CP-S067", "chunk_id": "CP-S067-0010", "chunk_index": 9, "publisher": "NVIDIA Careers", "title": "University Recruiting", "category": "internships", "topics": ["students", "internships"], "url": "https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/about-nvidia/careers/university-recruiting/", "resolved_url": "https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/about-nvidia/careers/university-recruiting/", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:56.417448+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "the next generation of corporate leaders. Through our best-in-class programs, we also provide powerful upleveling and organic growth tools to help professionals pivot industries and pursue lifelong learning. At NVIDIA, I was given the resources, autonomy, and unwavering support to push my limits and dream bigger than ever. My team not only challenged me but also lifted me up, helping me unlock potential I never imagined I could reach in just one summer. — Paul, MBA Intern PhDs at NVIDIA have the opportunity to make an impact across the company—not only within our world-class Research organization, but also in engineering, product, and other technical teams. Our researchers are advancing technology and publishing at top conferences, while many other teams apply cutting-edge methods to build real products, platforms, and services. Whether you’re passionate about pushing scientific discovery or applying research to solve real-world challenges, there’s a place for your expertise at NVIDIA. I had the opportunity to work on impactful projects closely aligned with my research interests, allowing me to both contribute meaningfully and deepen my technical expertise. — Swapnil, PhD Intern NVIDIA empowers everyone to contribute as you get your hands on the latest computing technology. Within our New College Graduate (NCG) program, you’ll be able to influence areas ranging from high-performance computing and graphics to edge computing, networking, autonomous machines, and more. We provide great benefits that include ESPP, tuition reimbursement, continuous learning and development programs, paid time off, and more. Our university students and early-in-career hires will one day become our future leaders—overseeing large teams, bringing innovative products to market, and making a difference by helping us take on the world’s greatest challenges. At NVIDIA, it’s unique how leadership isn’t restricted by title or seniority. I have the autonomy to guide my team toward shared goals. That’s not something that you expect to feel as an intern or new college graduate, and I felt that on day one. — Neha, Technical Security Product Manager Join Us at Our Upcoming Events Learn More Check Out These Additional Resources Benefits Explore the benefits and support programs available to help your physical, mental, and financial health. Explore NVIDIA Benefits Academic Programs Discover a hub of resources and news for researchers, educators, and students. Discover Our Academic Programs Teams in Action Learn about the breakthroughs we’re making here and how NVIDIA is impacting businesses everywhere. Meet Our Teams Hiring Areas Get an overview of general hiring areas at NVIDIA and the skills we’re looking for. Find Your Perfect Fit NVIDIA is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to fostering an inclusive environment. NVIDIA is committed to offering reasonable accommodations, upon request, to job applicants with disabilities. If you need"}
{"source_id": "CP-S067", "chunk_id": "CP-S067-0011", "chunk_index": 10, "publisher": "NVIDIA Careers", "title": "University Recruiting", "category": "internships", "topics": ["students", "internships"], "url": "https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/about-nvidia/careers/university-recruiting/", "resolved_url": "https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/about-nvidia/careers/university-recruiting/", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:56.417448+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 178, "text": "Programs Teams in Action Learn about the breakthroughs we’re making here and how NVIDIA is impacting businesses everywhere. Meet Our Teams Hiring Areas Get an overview of general hiring areas at NVIDIA and the skills we’re looking for. Find Your Perfect Fit NVIDIA is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to fostering an inclusive environment. NVIDIA is committed to offering reasonable accommodations, upon request, to job applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please contact Human Resources at 408-486-1405 or provide your contact information and we will contact you. Read NVIDIA’s Applicant Privacy Policy . Company Information About Us Investors Venture Capital (NVentures) NVIDIA Foundation Research Corporate Sustainability Technologies Careers News and Events Newsroom Company Blog Technical Blog Webinars Stay Informed Events Calendar GTC AI Conference NVIDIA On-Demand Popular Links Developers Partners Executive Insights Startups and VCs Documentation Technical Training Professional Services for Data Science Follow NVIDIA United States Privacy Policy Your Privacy Choices Terms of Service Accessibility Corporate Policies Product Security Contact Copyright © 2026 NVIDIA Corporation"}
{"source_id": "CP-S068", "chunk_id": "CP-S068-0001", "chunk_index": 0, "publisher": "IBM Careers", "title": "IBM Careers", "category": "employer", "topics": ["careers", "AI"], "url": "https://www.ibm.com/careers/us-en/", "resolved_url": "https://www.ibm.com/careers", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:56.583254+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html;charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "Define your career with IBM Home Careers Search jobs Join us and create incredible things that alter the future for us, for each other, for our clients and for the world. Search Jobs Career Areas From Research and Consulting to Software Engineering, bring your skills to any of our career areas and grow beyond limits. Careers here don’t follow a script. IBMers create real impact for clients, communities and each other, from innovation in quantum to Hybrid Cloud, mainframe to AI and beyond. Explore our Career Areas Entry Level Learn about our entry-level programs, including internships, and how you can shape your career and contribute to impactful projects. Explore Entry Level Opportunities Application Steps and Tips Find out what to expect every step of the way, and get helpful career guidance directly from recruiters and expert IBMers. Explore our Application Steps and Tips Life@IBM Culture Careers Blog Locations Alumni Culture Get to know life at IBM, including all the ways we celebrate innovation, make an impact through technology and empower IBMers. Explore our Culture Careers Blog Discover countless stories of impact, collaboration and experimentation, all led by the ingenuity of IBMers around the globe. Explore our Careers Blog Locations Take an inside look at what it’s like to join our team across the Americas, Europe, Asia Pacific, the Middle East and Africa. Explore our Locations Once an IBMer, always an IBMer Careers aren’t straight lines anymore. People grow, explore, take risks, change directions. Sometimes that means continuing your journey somewhere new. Your time here is not just a chapter you close. It’s something you carry with you in how you think, how you collaborate, and how you approach challenges. At IBM, we don’t see alumni as former employees, but as part of something broader. Whether you’ve just recently moved on or it’s been years, you’re still part of our story. Learn more about Alumni program “It’s amazing to see what can happen when trust is built and great minds collaborate. My two longest-standing inventing teams have transformed from a pure inventing engine to a mentorship team for other inventors. ” -PJ, Infrastructure, United States Discover more stories “I started at IBM as an intern. Today, I have 13 patents and lead an entire team of hardware engineers in our 5,000 sq. ft. semiconductor test facility.” -Akil, Infrastructure, United States Discover more stories “From software testing to cybersecurity, to quantum computing, my IBM journey has been about reinvention and helping others find the courage to do the same.” -Guncha, Infrastructure, India Discover more stories Keep exploring Talent Network Stay up to date on career related news and events. Join our Talent Network Job Alerts Get notified on job openings that match"}
