{"source_id": "CP-S086", "chunk_id": "CP-S086-0001", "chunk_index": 0, "publisher": "NSDC", "title": "National Skill Development Corporation", "category": "india", "topics": ["India", "skills"], "url": "https://www.nsdcindia.org/", "resolved_url": "https://www.nsdcindia.org/", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:58.574564+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) Home Learner Partners Schemes & Initiatives Pathways Research & Insights About Us Search Schemes ​ ​ Kaushal Bhawan, 5th-6th Floors New Moti Bagh, New Delhi – 110023 011 – 71600050 enquiry@nsdcindia.org Follow us on: Life at NSDC Careers Contact Us Grievance Tenders Press Releases Media Testimonials Reports Privacy Policy Terms of Use Cookie Policy Disclaimer Follow us on: Follow us on: © 2026 NSDC India. All rights reserved. Sitemap Go to top Skills and opportunities for all, anytime, anywhere < > About NSDC Established in 2008 as a Public-Private Partnership, the National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC), under the aegis of the Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship (MSDE), was created to strengthen India’s skilling ecosystem by bridging talent with opportunity. At the heart of NSDC is a simple belief that skills do more than just prepare people for work. They build confidence, inspire ambition and unlock the potential to achieve more. Every skill acquired opens a new possibility. Every opportunity realised transforms not just an individual, but families, businesses, communities and, ultimately, the nation. Know More Vision To unlock the potential of India's Human Capital through skills, addressing the defining challenge of the times. Mission To serve as India's National Institution enabling a unified public-private skills ecosystem that enhances industry's global competitiveness and empowers learners to lead lives of Dignity, Opportunity, and Resilience. How India Gets Ready To Rise We Prepare We create access to industry-relevant skills, quality training & nationally recognised certifications, helping every learner build the confidence to take the next step. We Connect Through employers, training partners, governments and industry, we connect talent with real opportunities where skills can create meaningful careers. We Enable By strengthening people, businesses and institutions alike, we're building a workforce that's ready for tomorrow and an India that's ready to lead. Our Footprint 2500+ National Qualification Packs 300K+ Skill Trainers 5+Cr. Candidates Trained Empowering millions through industry-relevant skilling, employment opportunities. 250K+ Specially-abled Trained 36 Sector Skill Councils 750+ Districts 198K+ Partners Collaborating with government, industry, training providers, and ecosystem partners. 1.9+Cr Women Trained 1.47Cr. Marginalised Socio-Economic Groups Our Pathways NSDC Academy Building accessible learning pathways with industry-aligned programs and expert-led training. NSDC Skill Financing Supporting government-led skill initiatives with scalable implementation and measurable outcomes. NSDC Insights Enabling catalytic capital, impact partnerships, and outcome-focused financing for skilling. NSDC Digital Transforming careers through digital-first skilling, certifications, and lifelong learning opportunities. NSDC International Connecting Indian talent with global opportunities through mobility, language, and readiness programs. NSDC Evolution 2008-2014 Institution Establishment Single apex institution in skill development space Funded the SSC / TP ecosystem Supported establishment of SSDMs Developed QP / NOS system 2015 – 2022 Platform Development Brought under the"}
{"source_id": "CP-S086", "chunk_id": "CP-S086-0002", "chunk_index": 1, "publisher": "NSDC", "title": "National Skill Development Corporation", "category": "india", "topics": ["India", "skills"], "url": "https://www.nsdcindia.org/", "resolved_url": "https://www.nsdcindia.org/", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:58.574564+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "measurable outcomes. NSDC Insights Enabling catalytic capital, impact partnerships, and outcome-focused financing for skilling. NSDC Digital Transforming careers through digital-first skilling, certifications, and lifelong learning opportunities. NSDC International Connecting Indian talent with global opportunities through mobility, language, and readiness programs. NSDC Evolution 2008-2014 Institution Establishment Single apex institution in skill development space Funded the SSC / TP ecosystem Supported establishment of SSDMs Developed QP / NOS system 2015 – 2022 Platform Development Brought under the aegis of MSDE Publicly-funded, scheme-driven scale-up (PMKVY /PM- NAPS) Creation of SDMS / Skill India Portal digital platform establishment 2022-2026 Platform Expansion Progression on digital platform – SIDH Focus on private-sector initiatives – NSDC Academy, NSDC International Convergence of several public skilling schemes on digital platform Schemes & Initiatives PMKVY (Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana) Empowering youth with industry-relevant skills for enhanced employability &amp; sustainable livelihoods. View PM Vishwakarma Supporting traditional artisans and craftspeople through skill enhancement &amp; financial assistance. View SIICs (Skill India International Centres) Preparing Indian talent for global careers through international skill standards and mobility pathways. View NEED (National Entrepreneurs Empowerment Drive) Nurturing aspiring entrepreneurs with skills, mentorship, business support, and innovation opportunities. View View All News & Updates 19 Feb 2026 Emerging Talent from Western States Showcases Excellence at IndiaSkills West Regional Competition 2025–26 The IndiaSkills Regional Competition 2025-26 for the western states concluded at Gujarat National Law University, Gandhinagar, marking a successful celebration of talent, technical excellence, and regional pride. Organised under the IndiaSkills initiative of the Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship (MSDE) and supported by the National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC), knowledge partner and implementation partner for IndiaSkills Competition 2025–26, the competition brought together more than 300+ skilled youth from five western states, including Gujarat, Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Rajasthan, and Goa, competing across 63 skill categories aligned with national and global industry standards. 27 Mar 2025 NSDC, IIT Mandi, and NCU Gurugram collaborate to offer a B.Tech course in semiconductor design and Technology National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC), IIT Mandi and the NorthCap University (NCU), Gurugram have today signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) to launch a B.Tech. ECE in Semiconductor Design and Technology programme. The agreement was formally signed today at Kaushal Bhawan, New Delhi. We have garnered 49 coverage acrossIndia including publications like India Today, Education Times(TOI), Times Now, Indian Express 27 Mar 2025 NSDC, IIT Mandi, and NCU Gurugram collaborate to offer a B.Tech course in semiconductor design and Technology National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC), IIT Mandi and the NorthCap University (NCU), Gurugram have today signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) to launch a B.Tech. ECE in Semiconductor Design and Technology programme. The agreement was formally signed today at Kaushal Bhawan, New Delhi. We have"}
{"source_id": "CP-S086", "chunk_id": "CP-S086-0003", "chunk_index": 2, "publisher": "NSDC", "title": "National Skill Development Corporation", "category": "india", "topics": ["India", "skills"], "url": "https://www.nsdcindia.org/", "resolved_url": "https://www.nsdcindia.org/", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:58.574564+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 396, "text": "publications like India Today, Education Times(TOI), Times Now, Indian Express 27 Mar 2025 NSDC, IIT Mandi, and NCU Gurugram collaborate to offer a B.Tech course in semiconductor design and Technology National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC), IIT Mandi and the NorthCap University (NCU), Gurugram have today signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) to launch a B.Tech. ECE in Semiconductor Design and Technology programme. The agreement was formally signed today at Kaushal Bhawan, New Delhi. We have garnered 49 coverage acrossIndia including publications like India Today, Education Times(TOI), Times Now, Indian Express 26 Mar 2025 NSDC partners with Axim Collaborative to enhance Open edX Platform, drive innovation in skill development National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) partnered with Axim Collaborative, a non-profit organization, to enhance the Open edX open-source software Platform and drive innovation in education and skill ecosystem to empower youths. We have garnered 134 coverage across India. 26 Mar 2025 NSDC partners with Axim Collaborative to enhance Open edX Platform, drive innovation in skill development National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) partnered with Axim Collaborative, a non-profit organization, to enhance the Open edX open-source software Platform and drive innovation in education and skill ecosystem to empower youths. We have garnered 134 coverage across India. 18 Mar 2025 Coverage Dossier_ NSDC setting up Centre for Future Skills at Chaudhary Charan Singh Univers The National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) is setting up a state-of-the-art Centre for Future Skills, under NSDC Academy, at Chaudhary Charan Singh University (CCSU), Meerut to empower youth in new technology courses like Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Internet of Things, Healthcare/Paramedical, and Languages. In addition to this, the Sports Physical Education Fitness and Leisure Skills Council (SPEFL-SC) is also establishing a Manufacturing-cum-Training facility at CCSU, funded through CSR initiatives. We have garnered 24 coverage across India. 18 Mar 2025 Coverage Dossier_ NSDC setting up Centre for Future Skills at Chaudhary Charan Singh Univers The National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) is setting up a state-of-the-art Centre for Future Skills, under NSDC Academy, at Chaudhary Charan Singh University (CCSU), Meerut to empower youth in new technology courses like Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Internet of Things, Healthcare/Paramedical, and Languages. In addition to this, the Sports Physical Education Fitness and Leisure Skills Council (SPEFL-SC) is also establishing a Manufacturing-cum-Training facility at CCSU, funded through CSR initiatives. We have garnered 24 coverage across India. View All Success Stories All No Data Found"}
