Programming and Software Engineering Fundamentals Duke University Beginner 3 - 6 Months 4.6 (22,238) No prerequisites 3 Applied Software Engineering Fundamentals IBM Beginner 3 - 6 Months 4.6 (52,089) No prerequisites Frequently Asked Questions about Software Engineering What is software engineering? â Software engineering is the practice of designing, building, testing, and maintaining software in a structured and reliable way. It combines programming with problem-solving, system design, collaboration, quality assurance, and development workflows. Courses such as IBMâs Introduction to Software Engineering and The Hong Kong University of Science and Technologyâs Software Engineering can help you understand how software projects move from requirements to working applications. On Coursera, you can choose introductory or more applied courses depending on whether you want a broad overview or hands-on development practice. â What jobs use software engineering? â Software engineering is used in roles that involve building, improving, testing, or operating software systems. Common examples include software developer, full-stack developer, backend developer, frontend developer, application developer, DevOps engineer , quality assurance tester, and technical support engineer. Programs such as IBM Full Stack Software Developer, Microsoft Full-Stack Developer, and IBM DevOps and Software Engineering connect software engineering concepts with practical development and deployment workflows. Coursera courses can help you explore these role areas while building skills in programming, version control, application development, and software delivery. â What skills should I learn before software engineering?"}
{"source_id": "CP-S094", "chunk_id": "CP-S094-0005", "chunk_index": 4, "publisher": "Coursera", "title": "Software Engineering Courses", "category": "learning", "topics": ["software engineering", "learning"], "url": "https://www.coursera.org/courses?query=software%20engineering", "resolved_url": "https://www.coursera.org/courses?query=software%20engineering", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:55:59.875877+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html", "word_count": 450, "text": "full-stack developer, backend developer, frontend developer, application developer, DevOps engineer , quality assurance tester, and technical support engineer. Programs such as IBM Full Stack Software Developer, Microsoft Full-Stack Developer, and IBM DevOps and Software Engineering connect software engineering concepts with practical development and deployment workflows. Coursera courses can help you explore these role areas while building skills in programming, version control, application development, and software delivery. â What skills should I learn before software engineering? â Before learning software engineering, it helps to understand basic programming, problem-solving, and how computers run software. You do not need to know everything in advance, but familiarity with variables, functions, data structures, and command-line basics can make the learning process smoother. Duke Universityâs Java Programming and Software Engineering Fundamentals is a useful option for learners who want to build programming foundations alongside software engineering concepts. If you are newer to the field, starting with an introductory course can help you build confidence before moving into full-stack or DevOps topics. â What skills complement software engineering? â Skills that complement software engineering include programming, data structures, databases , web development, cloud basics, testing, Git , DevOps , and communication. These skills help you build software that is not only functional, but also maintainable, collaborative, and easier to deploy. IBM DevOps and Software Engineering emphasizes development workflows and delivery practices, while Microsoft Full-Stack Developer and IBM Full Stack Software Developer support broader application-building skills. Courseraâs course selection can help you combine software engineering with related technical skills based on the kinds of projects you want to build. â How do I start learning software engineering? â A good way to start learning software engineering is to begin with core concepts, then practice by building small software projects. Start with an introductory course to learn how software is planned, designed, tested, and maintained, then add programming and development tools as you go. IBMâs Introduction to Software Engineering and Applied Software Engineering Fundamentals are relevant starting points, while Duke Universityâs Java Programming and Software Engineering Fundamentals can help you strengthen coding basics. On Coursera, you can follow a path from beginner concepts to hands-on full-stack or DevOps coursework. â Can I learn software engineering for free? â Yes. You can start learning software engineering on Coursera for free in two ways: Preview the first module of many software engineering courses at no cost. This includes video lessons, readings, graded assignments, and Coursera AI (where available). Start a 7-day free trial for Specializations or Coursera Plus. This gives you full access to all course content across eligible programs within the timeframe of your trial. If you want to keep learning, earn a certificate in software engineering, or unlock full"}
