{"source_id": "CP-S096", "chunk_id": "CP-S096-0001", "chunk_index": 0, "publisher": "edX", "title": "Computer Science", "category": "learning", "topics": ["computer science", "learning"], "url": "https://www.edx.org/learn/computer-science", "resolved_url": "https://www.edx.org/learn/computer-science", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:56:00.414503+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "Computer science courses online | edX Learn edX For Business Home learn Learn computer science online Learn computer science online Research university-developed edX computer science courses to find those that align with your education and career goals. Create an account Key takeaways edX's online computer science courses and programs cover programming languages, cybersecurity, and data science. Six-to-eight-week executive education programs can help you combine your computer science expertise with in-demand management skills. edX individual courses start at just $50 if you want to earn a certificate upon completion. Popular online computer science courses with certificates Career of a Software Developer Microsoft Course Computer Science for Artificial Intelligence Harvard University Professional Certificate 2 courses Mastering Generative AI for Software Development IBM Course CS50's Introduction to Computer Science Harvard University Course Show More What is computer science? Computer science focuses on applying computing, algorithms, and programming techniques to operating systems, artificial intelligence (AI), and informatics. Languages like Python are widely used across these areas. Advances in machine learning, AI, and cybersecurity have led to growth in information technology. Computers are used in nearly all fields of study and professions. Computer scientists create systems designed to understand big data structures, operationalize tasks, and innovate for the future. As algorithms become more complex, the computer science field is expanding to include more subfields and concentrations. Enrolling in an online course or degree program can be worth it to help you learn programming languages, explore principles of computer science, and gain new skills. Why learn computer science? You can qualify for opportunities in a high-growth field: The Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS) projects nearly 318,000 annual job openings in computer and information technology from 2024 to 2034. By studying computer science, you can become a problem-solver in high-impact fields like healthcare, cybersecurity, education, urban development, and many others. In a 2025 edX survey, 36% of leaders listed AI and machine learning as a top skill for career advancement, 25% listed software development, 23% listed cybersecurity, and 14% listed cloud computing — all skills that require computer science expertise, often taught using languages like Browse computer science courses Browse online Computer Science certificates Find new interests and advance your career opportunities Stand out in your field Use the knowledge and skills you have gained to drive impact at work and grow your career. Learn at your own pace On your computer, tablet or phone, online courses make learning flexible to fit your busy life. Earn a valuable credential Showcase your key skills and valuable knowledge. Certificates (197) Courses (863) Executive Education (21) Bachelor's Programs (1) Certificates Computer Science for Python Programming Harvard University Professional Certificate 2 courses Computer Science for Cybersecurity Harvard University Professional Certificate 2"}
