ions at different price points. Compare them to chart your education journey. Program type Who is it best for? Typical duration Cost range What you can learn Course Professionals without a computer science background 2-4 weeks Starts at ~$50 Computer science and business, Image generation, Programming Professional certificate New and experienced professionals wanting to improve their résumé 2-10 months Starts at ~$500 Python programming, Databases, Computer science fundamentals Executive education Current and aspiring managers 6-8 weeks Starts at ~$2,500 Artificial intelligence (AI) and healthcare Bachelor's program Recent high school graduates wanting to qualify for entry-level positions 4-6 years Starts at ~$10,000 Data science, Computer science, Programming Master's program Experienced professionals working toward a promotion 1-3 years Starts at ~$10,000 AI, Algorithm design, Data management Course Who is it best for? Professionals without a computer science background Typical duration 2-4 weeks Cost range Starts at ~$50 What you can learn Computer science and business, Image generation, Programming Professional certificate Who is it best for? New and experienced professionals wanting to improve their résumé Typical duration 2-10 months Cost range Starts at ~$500 What you can learn Python programming, Databases, Computer science fundamentals Executive education Who is it best for? Current and aspiring managers Typical duration 6-8 weeks Cost range Starts at ~$2,500 What you can learn Artificial intelligence (AI) and healthcare Bachelor's program Who is it best for? Recent high school graduates wanting to qualify for entry-level positions Typical duration 4-6 years Cost range"}
{"source_id": "CP-S096", "chunk_id": "CP-S096-0005", "chunk_index": 4, "publisher": "edX", "title": "Computer Science", "category": "learning", "topics": ["computer science", "learning"], "url": "https://www.edx.org/learn/computer-science", "resolved_url": "https://www.edx.org/learn/computer-science", "retrieval_method": "direct", "fetched_at": "2026-09-21T14:56:00.414503+00:00", "http_status": 200, "content_type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "word_count": 450, "text": "to improve their résumé Typical duration 2-10 months Cost range Starts at ~$500 What you can learn Python programming, Databases, Computer science fundamentals Executive education Who is it best for? Current and aspiring managers Typical duration 6-8 weeks Cost range Starts at ~$2,500 What you can learn Artificial intelligence (AI) and healthcare Bachelor's program Who is it best for? Recent high school graduates wanting to qualify for entry-level positions Typical duration 4-6 years Cost range Starts at ~$10,000 What you can learn Data science, Computer science, Programming Master's program Who is it best for? Experienced professionals working toward a promotion Typical duration 1-3 years Cost range Starts at ~$10,000 What you can learn AI, Algorithm design, Data management FAQ Frequently Asked Questions Can I learn computer science on my own? Yes, you can learn computer science on your own by taking advantage of free or low-cost instructional resources, like video lectures and tutorials. As some employers prioritize hard, demonstrable skills over formal educational credentials, you should consider validating the skills you gain by earning a professional certificate. Is computer science full of math? Computer science draws extensively on mathematics, but to describe it as \"full of math\" overlooks some key considerations. Many areas of computer science use algebra, calculus, discrete math, and statistics. The extent to which you use these mathematical branches in your studies or job duties varies by specialization and role. Schools and programs also use various strategies to teach computer science, and some approaches involve less math than others. Will AI replace computer science? Artificial intelligence might automate some entry-level computer science roles, particularly in areas like coding and basic programming. However, fears that AI systems will completely replace human computer science professionals do not align with the expert consensus. Instead, AI might change the way computer scientists conduct their research and perform their job duties, rather than eliminating human roles. Is a computer science degree worth it? A computer science degree can help you qualify for high-paying and high-growth career opportunities. These programs also emphasize versatile, valuable technical skills that transfer well across many industries. From this perspective, a computer science degree often offers a strong return on investment. Skills Python Artificial Intelligence (AI) Trading Data Analysis Finance Excel Data Science Software Engineering Project Management Machine Learning see more Courses Professional Certificates Harvard University's CS50 MicroMasters Programs MicroBachelors Programs XSeries Programs Certificates in AI Certificates in Project Management Certificates in Data Analytics Certificates in IT see more Certificates Online Degrees Bachelor's in Computer Science / Data Science Bachelor's in Psychology Bachelor's in Finance Bachelor's in Business Master's in Business Administration Master's in Statistics Master's in AI Master's in Data Science see more Undergraduate Degrees see more"}
